From a60628c245a85bf225085129efd030f2d574cfa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azathothas <ajamx101@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:40:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] warp up: the failure names each cause once, in one line

GitHub #738. The failure of warp up printed the error of the child, then
the same text again after "podnet warp proxy --detach exited 69:". The
line named the relay and the front door several times.

- warp::up::start keeps the error lines of the child (podnet: ...) until
  a log line comes after them. After a failure, the error of this
  process carries the cause and the steps of the child once. Before, the
  last line of the child was the cause, so a step line took its place.
- The relay leg of WARP (src/warp/relay_dial.rs, moved out of
  src/warp/mod.rs) gives the cause alone, at the stage relay: pod-warp
  names the door and the relay. An IPv6 door is "the relay has no IPv6
  egress".
- ws_relay::connect names the hosts of the relay that failed with the
  same words together, and each cause once.
- exit::tidy names a way out ("through the relay URL", "through the
  proxy URL") once in a line. The repeat comes from pod-warp
  (open.rs:109 joins "and through the relay NAME" before the failure of
  the leg, and session.rs:237 starts that failure with "TCP to the MASQUE
  front door DOOR through LABEL").

Tests: warp::relay_dial::tests::a_failure_through_the_relay_names_each_cause_once,
warp::up::tests::the_error_of_the_child_is_said_once, and a case of
exit::tests::tidy_says_each_part_once_and_no_debug_form.
